I always confused with APRS. I believe people use the term "APRS" interchangeably with "Positioning report". Sometimes they can have APRS over DMR, most of the times they refer to FM, VHF/AFSK/AX.25/APRS. I, personally operate APRS mostly on 144.39Mhz (FM) and 10.1478Mhz (USB).<br><br>Now, I'm very confused when trying to put "APRS" on the layers. <br><br>So, I'm trying to put "APRS" on the OST layers model to be able to understand it. please help me, I'm not quite sure what I'm doing. Which layer is the APRS, I can't put it. OR it is not a protocol to begin with?<br><br>VHF FM APRS (144.390 in the US.)<br>OSI layers<br>7 (Application)<br>6 (Presentation)<br>5 (session)<br>4 (Transport)<br>3 (Network) <br>2 (DATALINK) ---&gt; AFSK / AX.25 / FM<br>1 (Physical) ---&gt; VHF RF<br><br>HF USB APRS (10.1478)<br>7 (Application)<br>6 (Presentation)<br>5 (session)<br>4 (Transport)<br>3 (Network) <br>2 (DATALINK) ---&gt; AFSK / AX.25 / USB<br>1 (Physical) ---&gt; HF RF<br><br>UHF DMR APRS<br>7 (Application)<br>6 (Presentation)<br>5 (session)<br>4 (Transport)<br>3 (Network) <br>2 (DATALINK) ---&gt; FM / TDMA<br>1 (Physical) ---&gt; UHF RF<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Tue May 27, 2025 12:57 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
